# Middleware registration order

Register middleware only in `LifecycleManager._add_middlewares_in_order`. A middleware
class never installs itself.

Starlette: the last `app.add_middleware(...)` is outermost. It sees the request first
and the response last.

Order in that method, innermost first:

1. `PrometheusManager.add_middleware(app)` — Prometheus. Measures the application.
2. `CorrelationIdMiddleware` — outermost, so every inner log line has
   `correlation_id` and every response carries `X-Request-ID`.

FastMCP's `RequestContextMiddleware` is already on the app from `http_app()` and stays
closer to the application than these two.

`PrometheusManager.add_metrics_router(app, config)` mounts `GET /metrics`.
Call it after `_add_middlewares_in_order`, once `http_app()` has returned.

Do not call a library's `instrument(app)` / `setup(app)` after this method or after
`create_app()` returns. Those helpers often call `add_middleware` implicitly.
That silently becomes the new outermost layer.

Do not wrap the app in `main` (`app = SomeASGIWrapper(app)`). That wrapper sits
outside this middleware stack. If the library must participate in this order,
register it in `_add_middlewares_in_order` in the intended slot.
